{"ts":"2026-11-15T19:55:42.768Z","tool":"execute_code","type":"tool","status":"ERROR","ms":1143,"action":"execute","params":{"action":"execute","code":"var sb = new System.Text.StringBuilder();\n\n// 1. Copy missing textures & float/color params from Terrain Splat.mat onto Underwater Plateau *.mat\nvar splat = AssetDatabase.LoadAssetAtPath<Material>(\"Assets/Materials/Terrain/Terrain Splat.mat\");\nstring[] platPaths = {\n    \"Assets/Materials/Island/Underwater Plateau Surface.mat\",\n    \"Assets/Materials/Island/Underwater Plateau Escarpment.mat\",\n    \"Assets/Materials/Island/Underwater Plateau Formations.mat\"\n};\nstring[] texProps = { \"_RockAlbedo\", \"_RockNormal\", \"_SandAlbedo\", \"_SandNormal\", \"_SeabedAlbedo\", \"_SeabedNormal\", \"_GrassAlbedo\", \"_GrassNormal\" };\nstring[] fltProps = { \"_RockTiling\", \"_RockNormalScale\", \"_SandTiling\", \"_SandNormalScale\", \"_SeabedTiling\", \"_SeabedNormalScale\", \"_SeabedSmoothness\", \"_GrassTiling\", \"_MacroTiling\", \"_MacroStrength\" };\n\nif (splat != null)\n{\n    sb.AppendLine(\"TerrainSplat _UseSurfaceTint=\" + splat.GetFloat(\"_UseSurfaceTint\"));\n    for (int i = 0; i < platPaths.Length; i++)\n    {\n        var pm = AssetDatabase.LoadAssetAtPath<Material>(platPaths[i]);\n        if (pm == null) continue;\n        for (int t = 0; t < texProps.Length; t++)\n            if (pm.HasProperty(texProps[t]) && splat.HasProperty(texProps[t]))\n                pm.SetTexture(texProps[t], splat.GetTexture(texProps[t]));\n        for (int f = 0; f < fltProps.Length; f++)\n            if (pm.HasProperty(fltProps[f]) && splat.HasProperty(fltProps[f]))\n                pm.SetFloat(fltProps[f], splat.GetFloat(fltProps[f]));\n        if (pm.HasProperty(\"_SeabedTint\") && splat.HasProperty(\"_SeabedTint\"))\n            pm.SetColor(\"_SeabedTint\", splat.GetColor(\"_SeabedTint\"));\n        EditorUtility.SetDirty(pm);\n        sb.AppendLine(\"Synced textures to \" + platPaths[i]);\n    }\n}\n\n// 2. Check sample SurfaceTint center/corner pixel on an Island chunk vs Plateau chunk\nvar grids = UnityEngine.Object.FindObjectsOfType<MapGrid>();\nfor (int i = 0; i < grids.Length; i++)\n{\n    var mr = grids[i].GetComponent<MeshRenderer>();\n    var pb = new MaterialPropertyBlock();\n    mr.GetPropertyBlock(pb);\n    var st = pb.GetTexture(\"_SurfaceTint\") as Texture2D;\n    var ctrl = pb.GetTexture(\"_Control\") as Texture2D;\n    string sn = mr.sharedMaterial != null ? mr.sharedMaterial.shader.name : \"\";\n    if (st != null && i < 6)\n    {\n        sb.AppendLine(grids[i].name + \" (\" + sn + \"): SurfaceTint(corner)=\" + st.GetPixel(1, 1)\n            + \" Ctrl(corner)=\" + (ctrl != null ? ctrl.GetPixel(1, 1).ToString() : \"null\")\n            + \" UseST=\" + pb.GetFloat(\"_UseSurfaceTint\")\n            + \" SeabedTexPB=\" + (pb.GetTexture(\"_SeabedAlbedo\") != null ? pb.GetTexture(\"_SeabedAlbedo\").name : \"null\"));\n    }\n}\n\n// 3. Turn off _SOFTPARTICLES_ON on Vent*.mat and save assets so particles render cleanly across any camera!\nstring[] vfxMats = {\n    \"Assets/Resources/VFX/VentMineralPlume.mat\",\n    \"Assets/Resources/VFX/VentThermalCoreGlow.mat\",\n    \"Assets/Resources/VFX/VentRisingBubbles.mat\"\n};\nfor (int i = 0; i < vfxMats.Length; i++)\n{\n    var vm = AssetDatabase.LoadAssetAtPath<Material>(vfxMats[i]);\n    if (vm == null) continue;\n    if (vm.HasProperty(\"_SoftParticlesEnabled\")) vm.SetFloat(\"_SoftParticlesEnabled\", 0f);\n    vm.DisableKeyword(\"_SOFTPARTICLES_ON\");\n    vm.DisableKeyword(\"_FADING_ON\");\n    EditorUtility.SetDirty(vm);\n    sb.AppendLine(\"Updated VFX mat \" + vfxMats[i] + \" keywords=\" + string.Join(\",\", vm.shaderKeywords));\n}\nAssetDatabase.SaveAssets();\nreturn sb.ToString();\n","safety_checks":true,"compiler":"codedom"},"error":"Runtime error: Texture 'Generated Terrain Surface Tint' is not readable, the texture memory can not be accessed from scripts. You can make the texture readable in the Texture Import